From 518fb6f7bcc84e68cced84f58e2813f24d9a8e10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juan Manuel Lopez Carrillo <juanmanuellopezcarrillo@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 03:34:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 126/130] config: enable INPUT_JOYDEV=y (the sticks of the
 AN1 gamepad mapper)

The aurealnix-gamemap is designed joydev-first (/dev/input/jsN, JSIOCG*
ioctls, axes normalized to +-32767 via absinfo); without joydev it falls back
to raw evdev, where HID pads like the "Twin USB Joystick" emit the sticks in
0..255 and the mapper thresholds/sensitivity never trigger: buttons and D-pad
(HAT +-1) work, the sticks do not (dead mouse/aiming in web games). The other
AN1 boards already carry joydev; built-in like evdev.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .config | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/.config b/.config
index 0afbae6d2..9365910a8 100644
--- a/.config
+++ b/.config
@@ -3222,7 +3222,7 @@ CONFIG_INPUT_VIVALDIFMAP=y
 # Userland interfaces
 #
 # CONFIG_INPUT_MOUSEDEV is not set
-# CONFIG_INPUT_JOYDEV is not set
+CONFIG_INPUT_JOYDEV=y
 CONFIG_INPUT_EVDEV=y
 
 #
